#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:2
msgid "Manufacturing"
msgstr "制造"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:15
msgid ""
"Manufacturing is how the object comes to exist: which of its parts are "
"bought and which are made, how each made part is made and from what, what "
"the machines that make it are told, and in what order it all goes together. "
"PartCAD keeps that in the same declaration as the design, so the part that "
"is ordered is the part that was analysed, and the instructions are written "
"from the assembly they put together."
msgstr ""
"制造讲的是这个对象如何变成现实：它的哪些零件是买来的、哪些是自制的，每一个自制零件是怎么做的、由什么做的，制造它的那些机床被告知了什么，以及这一切按什么顺序装到一起。PartCAD"
" 把这些内容与设计放在同一份声明里，所以被订购的那个零件就是被分析过的那个零件，而装配说明也是从它们所装出来的那个装配体写出来的。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:23
msgid "What PartCAD captures"
msgstr "PartCAD 记录了什么"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:26
msgid "Whether it is made at all"
msgstr "它到底是否要被制造"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:28
msgid ""
"``manufacturable:`` says whether an object is something anybody is going to "
"make or buy -- on the object, or for a whole package. A model of something "
"somebody else makes, an import kept as it arrived, a scene: these are "
"records, and say ``manufacturable: false``. Everything else is held to what "
"follows."
msgstr ""
"``manufacturable:`` 说明某个对象是否是会有人去制造或采购的东西 -- "
"可以写在对象上，也可以为整个包写一次。别人制造的东西的模型、保持原样的导入件、场景：这些都是记录，应当声明 ``manufacturable: "
"false`` 。其他一切都要受下面各条的约束。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:34
msgid "Bought"
msgstr "采购"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:36
msgid ""
"A part or an assembly that is bought names who sells it, by ``vendor:`` and "
"``sku:``, and suppliers that carry it are found and asked for quotes by ``pc"
" supply``. An assembly that is sold assembled is ordered as one item, and "
"nothing inside it is looked at. See :ref:`procurement`."
msgstr ""
"采购来的零件或装配体会用 ``vendor:`` 和 ``sku:`` 指名是谁卖它的，而 ``pc supply`` "
"会找出有货的供应商并向他们询价。整装出售的装配体会作为一个条目来订购，而它内部的东西一概不再过问。参见 :ref:`procurement` 。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:42
msgid "Made"
msgstr "自制"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:44
msgid ""
"A part that is made says how, in a ``manufacturing:`` section: the method "
"(``additive``, ``subtractive``, ``forming``, ``sheet_metal``), the stock it "
"is made from (``source:``), the machines it is cut on (``cnc:``, ``laser:``,"
" ``drill:``, ``cut:``) and what they are told, and the tolerance it is made "
"to. See :ref:`made-from-stock`, :ref:`subtractive` and :ref:`sheet-metal`. "
"What it is made of is its :ref:`material <materials>`; the firmware a board "
"is flashed with is its :ref:`software <software>`."
msgstr ""
"自制的零件会在 ``manufacturing:`` 小节中说明怎么做：方式（ ``additive`` 、 ``subtractive`` 、 "
"``forming`` 、 ``sheet_metal`` ）、它所用的坯料（ ``source:`` ）、切削它的那些机床（ ``cnc:`` 、 "
"``laser:`` 、 ``drill:`` 、 ``cut:`` ）以及它们被告知的内容，还有它要做到的公差。参见 :ref:`made-from-"
"stock` 、 :ref:`subtractive` 和 :ref:`sheet-metal` 。它由什么做成是它的 :ref:`材料 "
"<materials>` ；烧进某块板子的固件则是它的 :ref:`软件 <software>` 。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:53
msgid "Put together"
msgstr "装到一起"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:55
msgid ""
"An assembly is put together by following its own Assembly YAML file: each "
"link says what it is joined to and how -- pushed, snapped or screwed in -- "
"so the steps can be written out for a person to follow (see :ref:`how an "
"assembly is manufactured <assembly-manufacturing>` and :doc:`/assy`)."
msgstr ""
"装配体是按它自己的 Assembly YAML 文件来装起来的：每一条链接都说明它与什么接合以及如何接合 -- 压入、卡入还是拧入 -- "
"这样各个步骤就能写出来供人照着做（参见 :ref:`装配体是如何制造出来的 <assembly-manufacturing>` 和 "
":doc:`/assy` ）。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:61
msgid "In the UI"
msgstr "在界面中"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:63
msgid ""
"**Manufacturing** has five tabs, for a part or an assembly; for a scene, a "
"sketch or an interface the whole group is disabled. They are in the order "
"they are decided, and the first decides the rest. Each has a chapter of its "
"own:"
msgstr ""
"**Manufacturing** "
"对零件或装配体有五个标签页；而对场景、草图或接口，整个这一组都是禁用的。它们按被决定的先后顺序排列，而第一个决定其余的。每一个都有自己的一章："

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:67
msgid ":doc:`Build vs Buy </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bvb>`"
msgstr ":doc:`Build vs Buy </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bvb>`"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:68
msgid ""
"Everything the object is made of, and on each a switch: build it, or buy it."
" The one decision in the Digital Thread that is kept on the machine of "
"whoever made it rather than in the package -- and the one that decides the "
"other four tabs."
msgstr ""
"该对象所由之构成的一切，而每一项上都有一个开关：自制，还是采购。这是 Digital Thread "
"中唯一一项保存在做出它的那个人的机器上、而不是保存在包里的决定 -- 也是决定了其余四个标签页的那一项。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:73
msgid ":doc:`Build </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build>`"
msgstr ":doc:`Build </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build>`"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:74
msgid ""
"What is built, in the order it is built in, each step a page of the "
"instructions -- with the machine route drawn where a part declares one."
msgstr "哪些东西是自制的，按它们被制造的顺序排列，每一个步骤一页说明 -- 而在某个零件声明了机床加工路径时，还会把那条路径画出来。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:77
msgid ":doc:`Buy </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_buy>`"
msgstr ":doc:`Buy </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_buy>`"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:78
msgid ""
"What is bought: where each line can be obtained, and a quote per supplier."
msgstr "哪些东西是采购的：每一个条目可以从哪里得到，以及每个供应商各给一份报价。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:80
msgid ":doc:`Bill of Materials </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom>`"
msgstr ""
":doc:`Bill of Materials </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom>`"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:81
msgid ""
"What has to be procured in order to have it, counted -- a made part as the "
"stock it is cut from."
msgstr "为了拥有它而必须采购的东西，并计数 -- 自制的零件按它所由之切出的坯料来计。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:84
msgid ":doc:`Assembly </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly>`"
msgstr ":doc:`Assembly </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly>`"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:85
msgid "The assembly instruction book, page by page, to read or save."
msgstr "装配说明书，一页一页地看，或者保存下来。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:87
msgid "The Manufacturing group: its five tabs, open on Build vs Buy"
msgstr "Manufacturing 组：它的五个标签页，当前打开在 Build vs Buy 上"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:94
msgid "On the command line"
msgstr "在命令行中"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:96
msgid "``pc bom`` lists everything the object takes, with how many of each."
msgstr "``pc bom`` 列出该对象所需要的一切，以及每一种各需要几个。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:97
msgid ""
"``pc supply find``, ``quote`` and ``order`` find suppliers, ask them for "
"prices and order from them -- see :ref:`providers and suppliers <supply-"
"chain>`."
msgstr ""
"``pc supply find`` 、 ``quote`` 和 ``order`` 用来找供应商、向他们询价并向他们下单 -- 参见 "
":ref:`提供方与供应商 <supply-chain>` 。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:99
msgid ""
"``pc instructions`` writes the assembly instructions: a page per step, each "
"drawn. It reads the **Build vs Buy** choices made on this machine, which is "
"what makes it write the steps for what *you* are building rather than for "
"everything the package could build."
msgstr ""
"``pc instructions`` 写出装配说明：每个步骤一页，每一页都画出来。它会读取本机上所做的 **Build vs Buy** "
"选择，正是这一点让它写出的是 *你* 正在构建的那些步骤，而不是这个包所能构建的一切。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:103
msgid ""
"``pc cam`` writes the programs the machines cut a part with -- see "
":ref:`machine routes <cam-routes>` for what it produces and what it cannot, "
"and :ref:`pc cam <cam>` for the command."
msgstr ""
"``pc cam`` 写出机床切削某个零件所用的那些程序 -- 它能产出什么、不能产出什么见 :ref:`机床加工路径 <cam-routes>` "
"，而命令本身见 :ref:`pc cam <cam>` 。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:106
msgid ""
"``pc info`` reports the material, the stock and the tolerances an object "
"resolved to, which is where a surprising bill of materials line is "
"explained."
msgstr "``pc info`` 报告某个对象所解析到的材料、坯料和各项公差，而一条让人意外的物料清单条目正是在这里得到解释的。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:110
msgid "How manufacturing is checked"
msgstr "制造是如何被检查的"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:112
msgid ""
"``pc test`` asks of every manufacturable object what ``pc supply`` would "
"order and what ``pc instructions`` would tell somebody to do: the "
"``manufacturability`` check, and one for each method -- additive, "
"subtractive, forming, sheet metal, and the laser, drill and cut machines -- "
"plus ``cam``, whether the route a machine is to cut it with can be produced."
" See :doc:`/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing`."
msgstr ""
"``pc test`` 会就每一个可制造对象询问 ``pc supply`` 会去订购什么、``pc instructions`` 会叫人做什么：也就是"
" ``manufacturability`` 检查，以及针对每一种方式各一项检查 -- 增材、减材、成形、钣金，以及激光、钻孔和锯切机床 -- 再加上 "
"``cam`` ，也就是机床要用来切削它的那条加工路径能否生成出来。参见 "
":doc:`/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing` 。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:120
msgid "Agent skills"
msgstr "智能体技能"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:121
msgid "``/pc:validate``"
msgstr "``/pc:validate``"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:122
msgid ""
"Reads the bill of materials and the assembly instructions as part of giving "
"a requirement its verdict, which is the one skill that exercises this phase "
"end to end."
msgstr "在给某项需求下结论的过程中读取物料清单和装配说明，它是唯一一项把这个阶段端到端走完的技能。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:126
msgid "``/pc:export`` and ``/pc:convert``"
msgstr "``/pc:export`` 和 ``/pc:convert``"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:127
msgid ""
"Write the file a supplier or a machine is given, in the format it asks for."
msgstr "按供应商或机床所要求的格式，写出要交给它的那个文件。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing.rst:129
msgid ""
"Choosing what to build and what to buy is deliberately not something a skill"
" does: it is a decision about who has which machines, it is kept on the "
"machine of whoever made it rather than in the package, and it is the one "
"input to this phase that is nobody else's to guess."
msgstr ""
"选择什么自制、什么采购，有意不交给技能去做：这是一项关于谁手上有哪些机床的决定，它保存在做出它的那个人的机器上而不是保存在包里，而且它是这个阶段唯一一项不该由别人去猜的输入。"
